Given an array arr[] containing only 0 and 1. Find the minimum toggles (switch from 0 to 1 or vice-versa) required such the array become partitioned, i.e., it has first 0s then 1s.

class Solution {
    int minToggle(int[] arr) {
        int onesCount = 0;
        int toggles = 0;

        for (int num : arr) {
            if (num == 1) {
                onesCount++;
            } else {
                // If it is 0, choose the cheaper option:
                // 1. Flip this 0 to 1 (toggles + 1)
                // 2. Flip all previous 1s to 0 (onesCount)
                toggles = Math.min(toggles + 1, onesCount);
            }
        }
        
        return toggles;
    }
}
